WEBVTT

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.870
"Sorry, we're closing early today!
Come back soon!"

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:14.950
Okay, help me carry this.

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:22.910
It's been ten months since the mass
escapes from Tokyo 7th Prison.

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:27.870
"Leader Albert Trevor"

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:27.160
Dangerous criminals like bomber
Albert Trevor and thief

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:31.950
Saizo Kumogakure remain at large.

00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:37.410
But last night, another escaped
criminal was found dead.

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:45.660
"Criminals Commit a Crime
After Escaping, Then Suicide"

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:39.500
Strangely, the escaped criminals

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:42.910
seem to be committing crimes
and then committing suicide.

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:45.660
The authorities are continuing to investigate...

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:46.950
Hey!

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:49.370
We're celebrating Moriarty's
release from prison.

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:51.450
You need to help us--

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:53.120
Sherlock!

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:02.080
Sherlock!

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:03.660
Wanna join in?

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:06.000
"Wahoo! Mrs. Hudson"

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:06.000
Look! It's Mrs. Hudson!

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:13.580
This is her.

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:13.580
"Wahoo! Mrs. Hudson"

00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:16.750
Hey, we worked really hard on that!

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:53.450
"Welcome home, Moriarty!"

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:58.000
"Looking back on Saudade"

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:55.120
Welcome back, Moririn.

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:58.000
Glad to have you out of there.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:01.040
I really worried you, huh?

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:04.660
And I didn't expect you to throw me a party.

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:06.540
Thank you.

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:08.500
It's fine.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:11.790
You look like you've grown up a little.

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:13.200
Really?

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:15.120
Captain!

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:20.580
We protected Kabukicho while you were gone!

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:23.700
Thanks.

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:28.750
You got out pretty early.
How'd you pull that off?

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:32.290
Officially, it was self-defense.

00:03:32.290 --> 00:03:35.830
It looks like Dad tried to help me out.

00:03:35.830 --> 00:03:37.580
He's got that election coming up.

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:40.910
The rich families of the
West Side are incredible...

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:44.700
But what I did doesn't disappear.

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:47.370
From now on, I need to keep on atoning.

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:55.290
"Welcome home, Moriarty!"

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:53.080
Well, from now on, just be
a good upstanding citizen like me!

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:55.290
Yeah.

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:58.080
Everyone, help me carry the food.

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:00.950
Okay!

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:08.410
Moriarty, everything's just felt so empty
to me since you went to prison.

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:12.370
Of course, I think everyone
else felt the same way.

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:15.200
I'm glad you're back.

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:17.700
Welcome back, Moriarty.

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:22.290
Thanks, Watson.

00:04:22.290 --> 00:04:25.370
But you know, Sherlock's sure late...

00:04:25.370 --> 00:04:28.410
He always is.

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:36.330
"Welcome home, Moriarty!"

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:41.330
Congratulations!

00:04:41.330 --> 00:04:46.200
I'm spinning it faster than I usually do!

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:51.540
That's Bliking! You love Bliking!

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:52.870
And it's signed, too!

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:56.750
Wow, Sherlock never gives people presents.

00:04:56.750 --> 00:04:59.410
I've never seen it happen before.

00:04:59.410 --> 00:05:02.700
Hey, I want a present, too!

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:05.450
Shut up! Get lost!

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:08.000
Isn't that nice, Moriarty?

00:05:12.870 --> 00:05:15.000
Let's go to one more place, guys!

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:17.160
Yay!

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:19.540
It's time for kids to go to bed.

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:21.330
We're celebrating the
captain's release from prison.

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:22.790
Don't be like that.

00:05:22.790 --> 00:05:24.540
You suck.

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:27.330
Right, right.

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:29.500
You're coming, too, right, Sherlock?

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:37.250
Hey, Sherlock.

00:05:37.250 --> 00:05:39.750
You're not going back to the West Side?

00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:41.830
What's that mean?

00:05:41.830 --> 00:05:44.910
You might have a fun time there.

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:47.660
I saw a lot of stuff in prison.

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:51.330
So I thought you might
find some interesting things.

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:54.790
How are things with Moran?

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:56.290
We were able to overcome our misunderstanding.

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:58.290
It's fine now.

00:05:58.290 --> 00:06:02.290
I'm busy helping him with his election.

00:06:02.290 --> 00:06:04.000
Hey!

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:08.950
"Batting Center"

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:05.950
Let's go here next!

00:06:05.950 --> 00:06:08.950
"Karakuri Yashiki"

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:22.540
Okay, I'm gonna hit a home run!

00:06:22.540 --> 00:06:24.450
Good luck.

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:29.000
Bring it!

00:06:33.750 --> 00:06:35.830
That's strange...

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:39.370
Scribbles?

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:44.950
You should wait till it gets a little
closer so you keep good form.

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:51.160
"Home Run"

00:06:48.290 --> 00:06:51.160
Home Run! Congratulations!

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:52.700
Like that!

00:06:58.290 --> 00:07:01.500
Baseball's fun.

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:03.750
I see.

00:07:03.750 --> 00:07:06.160
Let me go!

00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:08.500
Come to the office! I'm calling the police!

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:10.250
I didn't do anything!

00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:12.250
Get lost, you old bitch!

00:07:12.250 --> 00:07:14.580
Calm down, everyone.

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:16.040
What happened?

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:20.660
"Sasuke's Wife"

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:20.660
These brats are writing
graffiti all over our stuff!

00:07:20.660 --> 00:07:22.290
Look!

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:24.080
That wasn't us!

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:26.290
We're way better artists!

00:07:26.290 --> 00:07:28.290
You can tell it to the police!

00:07:28.290 --> 00:07:30.290
Let me go!

00:07:33.040 --> 00:07:35.330
Sasuke!

00:07:35.330 --> 00:07:36.200
Beat feet!

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:38.370
Wait, damn it!

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:41.750
Sheesh...

00:07:41.750 --> 00:07:46.830
You need to make the people
who did it clean it up!

00:07:43.410 --> 00:07:46.830
"Batting Center Owner"

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:53.040
He's been like this the past
few months because of their graffiti.

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:56.040
Something bothering you?

00:07:56.040 --> 00:07:57.450
No.

00:08:10.290 --> 00:08:12.870
Welcome home, Master James.

00:08:12.870 --> 00:08:17.330
Carlyle. You didn't need to stay up that late.

00:08:15.910 --> 00:08:21.870
"House Steward"

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:21.870
Young master, you should at least try
to eat dinner with your father.

00:08:21.870 --> 00:08:24.290
Yes. I know.

00:08:26.830 --> 00:08:29.750
Father, do you have a moment?

00:08:29.750 --> 00:08:32.410
Enter.

00:08:32.410 --> 00:08:38.540
Um, do I need to get anything
ready for tomorrow's speech?

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:38.540
You don't need to do a damn thing.

00:08:38.540 --> 00:08:42.080
Just stand by my side. And do nothing else.

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:50.120
Father... I'm grateful to you.

00:09:06.910 --> 00:09:09.120
The kids are making graffiti everywhere?

00:09:09.120 --> 00:09:12.750
They wouldn't do that.

00:09:12.750 --> 00:09:14.660
I mean, maybe they would.

00:09:14.660 --> 00:09:17.330
You're basically their parent.

00:09:17.330 --> 00:09:19.330
So make them listen!

00:09:19.330 --> 00:09:21.660
Don't get so mad!

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:25.500
I'm dead serious. Do something!

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:25.500
Oh, my. She came all the way here?

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:28.790
Yeah. I'm not sure what to do.

00:09:33.620 --> 00:09:36.080
I don't think they did it.

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:39.410
Why don't we all find
the real criminal together?

00:09:39.410 --> 00:09:41.700
This isn't a charity.

00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:44.700
I don't work for no reward.

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:46.540
Fine. I'll pay.

00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:48.580
S Class, with bonus.

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:53.120
Do you have the money?

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:56.040
I'm getting a decent amount from helping my dad.

00:09:56.040 --> 00:09:58.370
And I don't have anything else to use it for.

00:09:58.370 --> 00:10:01.580
This is... class difference.

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:04.830
And if I catch the guy I get it back.

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:06.950
What do you mean?

00:10:06.950 --> 00:10:09.450
I'm going to be a detective too, this time.

00:10:09.450 --> 00:10:12.250
Where's this coming from?

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:15.660
This time, it's a real mystery!
Doesn't it seem fun?

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:20.040
Right, Sherlock?

00:10:23.910 --> 00:10:27.290
I always wanted one of these.

00:10:27.290 --> 00:10:31.750
It's a cutting-edge pager
and can do all kinds of things.

00:10:34.620 --> 00:10:36.660
Cutting edge, huh?

00:10:36.660 --> 00:10:40.000
"Home Run"

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:40.000
Careful, Sherlock!

00:10:43.040 --> 00:10:46.000
This drawing is fascinating.

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:49.160
How? It's just scribbles.

00:10:49.160 --> 00:10:52.450
Look. It's the same picture
over and over, on everything.

00:10:52.450 --> 00:10:55.580
Doesn't that seem suggestive of something?

00:10:55.580 --> 00:10:58.160
"Home Run"

00:10:56.540 --> 00:10:58.160
Hey, old lady!

00:11:06.410 --> 00:11:10.250
Follow my plan and catch the criminal.

00:11:10.250 --> 00:11:12.290
Don't screw it up.

00:11:12.290 --> 00:11:14.950
You know who did it?

00:11:14.950 --> 00:11:16.870
Of course I do.

00:11:16.870 --> 00:11:19.500
It's those kids.

00:11:19.500 --> 00:11:22.910
I'm not touching those filthy kids.

00:11:20.910 --> 00:11:22.910
'Sup?

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:25.410
That's why I talked to you.

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:27.790
I don't think they're the type to lie...

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:29.040
<i>Up the butt</i> !

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:37.620
The police refuse to do a thing.

00:11:37.620 --> 00:11:41.660
I failed to get a few of them because
Sasuke- <i>san</i> erases them so quickly.

00:11:41.660 --> 00:11:44.160
No, this is plenty.

00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:47.040
Okay, lock up when you're done.

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:48.580
Got it.

00:11:50.370 --> 00:11:52.500
I've lined them up in order of date.

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:55.160
What's up with these, Sherlock?

00:11:55.160 --> 00:11:56.700
They're a code, dummy.

00:11:56.700 --> 00:11:58.830
What do you mean?

00:11:58.830 --> 00:12:01.410
Ever since they started showing up,

00:12:01.410 --> 00:12:05.790
the old guy's been desperate
to erase them immediately.

00:12:05.790 --> 00:12:11.870
Which means they contain something
he doesn't want anyone to know.

00:12:12.950 --> 00:12:15.040
But how do we crack it?

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:17.410
I already have.

00:12:17.410 --> 00:12:19.870
There are a bit over 40 types.

00:12:19.870 --> 00:12:21.790
I made the assumption that
they correspond to the letters

00:12:21.790 --> 00:12:24.160
of the Japanese alphabet, and put
them through a frequency analysis.

00:12:24.160 --> 00:12:28.120
It's like solving a crossword puzzle, basically.

00:12:28.120 --> 00:12:30.040
You did that just now?

00:12:30.040 --> 00:12:33.370
So what did it say?

00:12:33.370 --> 00:12:34.700
It's a threat.

00:12:34.700 --> 00:12:40.120
The message on the home run
target says "Kill tonight."

00:12:49.500 --> 00:12:51.330
Who could've done it?

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:00.910
What's it say?

00:13:00.910 --> 00:13:04.370
Midnight. Wait at elephant.

00:13:04.370 --> 00:13:08.870
If we ambush him there,
can we catch the guy who did it?

00:13:11.040 --> 00:13:12.870
That's right, Watson- <i>kun</i> !

00:13:12.870 --> 00:13:15.200
Smart thinking, Watson- <i>kun</i> !

00:13:15.200 --> 00:13:17.620
You're such a brilliant assistant!

00:13:17.620 --> 00:13:18.830
Now let's go!

00:13:18.830 --> 00:13:20.450
Yeah!

00:13:20.450 --> 00:13:22.790
Wait!

00:13:22.790 --> 00:13:24.000
What's gotten into you?

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:27.080
Hey, are you two listening?

00:13:27.080 --> 00:13:29.200
Don't leave me behind!

00:13:43.750 --> 00:13:46.200
Why're you erasing them?

00:13:48.410 --> 00:13:52.080
It's been a long time, Sasuke.

00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:53.830
Saizo!

00:13:53.830 --> 00:13:58.700
I sent you messages again and again.

00:13:55.250 --> 00:14:00.870
"Legendary Thief"

00:13:58.700 --> 00:14:00.870
Why don't you answer me?

00:14:00.870 --> 00:14:02.790
Why do you ignore me?

00:14:02.790 --> 00:14:05.830
I left the thieving business.

00:14:05.830 --> 00:14:09.580
And you're not going back to it?

00:14:11.080 --> 00:14:12.660
Listen, Sasuke.

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:15.330
Let's go back to how we used to be!

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:17.250
Working together!

00:14:24.950 --> 00:14:27.910
Grab on, Saizo!

00:14:27.910 --> 00:14:29.540
Sasuke!

00:14:37.370 --> 00:14:38.830
We did it!

00:14:38.830 --> 00:14:42.080
Yeah. There's nothing we can't steal!

00:14:42.080 --> 00:14:43.450
Yeah!

00:14:45.330 --> 00:14:46.160
This is the police!

00:14:46.160 --> 00:14:48.080
Give yourselves up!

00:14:49.660 --> 00:14:51.330
Go, Sasuke!

00:14:51.330 --> 00:14:52.160
But...

00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:53.620
Hurry!

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:57.250
Thanks!

00:15:03.160 --> 00:15:08.290
The only thing that kept me going
was the dream of doing

00:15:08.290 --> 00:15:11.700
one last big job with you!

00:15:11.700 --> 00:15:14.250
I'm grateful to you.

00:15:14.250 --> 00:15:17.910
Then come with me!

00:15:15.500 --> 00:15:17.910
Saizo, look at reality!

00:15:17.910 --> 00:15:20.290
High blood pressure. Rheumatism.

00:15:20.290 --> 00:15:24.620
We're hard of hearing.
Our bones break at the slightest fall.

00:15:24.620 --> 00:15:27.080
We're dried up old men!

00:15:27.080 --> 00:15:28.620
That's not true!

00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:30.330
I'm full of energy!

00:15:30.330 --> 00:15:31.200
I can still--

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:34.790
Give it up, you senile old man!

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:39.750
I see.

00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:45.200
You're not the man you once were.

00:15:45.200 --> 00:15:48.200
So...

00:15:48.200 --> 00:15:50.660
You can die here!

00:15:58.580 --> 00:16:01.910
S-Strike!

00:16:01.910 --> 00:16:03.700
What are you doing here?

00:16:03.700 --> 00:16:06.330
I thought I tricked you detectives into leaving!

00:16:06.330 --> 00:16:08.000
Um...

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:11.290
We've kind of been here the whole time.

00:16:11.290 --> 00:16:13.830
I-I knew that!

00:16:13.830 --> 00:16:18.120
Anyway, let's solve this
with dialogue, not violence!

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:19.910
Okay?

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:24.120
Then I'll kill you, too!

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:27.160
That's very dangerous, Grandpa!

00:16:27.160 --> 00:16:29.540
You'll hurt yourself!

00:16:29.540 --> 00:16:32.250
Stop moving so fast!

00:16:32.250 --> 00:16:33.750
Sorry!

00:16:39.500 --> 00:16:41.290
Well done, Watson.

00:16:41.290 --> 00:16:42.660
What a stupid farce.

00:16:42.660 --> 00:16:45.200
Help, don't watch!

00:16:47.080 --> 00:16:51.700
He really treasured those old memories, huh?

00:16:51.700 --> 00:16:55.080
What's going on here?

00:16:55.080 --> 00:16:55.910
Actually--

00:16:55.910 --> 00:17:02.370
Old man, weren't we leaving
to go ambush the criminal?

00:17:04.830 --> 00:17:07.410
The only ones who'd fall
for such an obvious trap

00:17:07.410 --> 00:17:11.410
are you and that moron over there.

00:17:11.410 --> 00:17:16.620
The message in the letter
was a trap to lure us away.

00:17:16.620 --> 00:17:20.790
Which means that we played along
to lure out the criminal?

00:17:20.790 --> 00:17:24.870
You're a cunning actor, old man.

00:17:24.870 --> 00:17:26.540
Right now, this old man, Sasuke,

00:17:26.540 --> 00:17:29.080
may just run a batting center.

00:17:29.080 --> 00:17:32.200
But he used to be a thief, and Saizo's partner.

00:17:32.200 --> 00:17:37.750
Those scribblings were a code they used
in their thieving days, most likely.

00:17:37.750 --> 00:17:42.250
Why did he kept sending so many messages?

00:17:42.250 --> 00:17:45.700
They were an attempt to get Sasuke
back into the thieving business.

00:17:45.700 --> 00:17:51.620
And a threat that if he didn't agree,
his past deeds would be revealed.

00:17:51.620 --> 00:17:55.160
That's why he was so desperate to erase them?

00:17:55.160 --> 00:17:59.410
He'd be in big trouble if somebody decoded them.

00:17:59.410 --> 00:18:00.620
Correct.

00:18:00.620 --> 00:18:02.200
I'm a criminal.

00:18:02.200 --> 00:18:04.120
Sasuke- <i>san</i> .

00:18:04.120 --> 00:18:09.250
How is a guy you're not friends
with anymore like a home run ball?

00:18:09.250 --> 00:18:11.700
I don't know, how?

00:18:11.700 --> 00:18:15.120
You ain't never seein' either again.

00:18:15.120 --> 00:18:18.000
That's all the time we have for today.

00:18:21.540 --> 00:18:23.330
I'm sorry, Saizo.

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:25.330
I can't go back to being a thief.

00:18:25.330 --> 00:18:29.040
I can't leave my wife.

00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:33.250
From now on, I'll do everything
I can to help you...

00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:41.580
Bullshit!

00:18:41.580 --> 00:18:43.410
I'm done with you!

00:18:43.410 --> 00:18:45.700
I'll do it all myself!

00:18:45.700 --> 00:18:48.370
I'll be a great thief!

00:18:56.750 --> 00:18:58.700
S-Saizo!

00:18:58.700 --> 00:19:00.410
Sasuke!

00:19:00.410 --> 00:19:02.040
Go after him!

00:19:02.040 --> 00:19:06.160
Please... stop Saizo!

00:19:16.500 --> 00:19:17.950
I did it!

00:19:17.950 --> 00:19:20.120
I did it just fine on my own!

00:19:21.410 --> 00:19:23.120
You stupid brats!

00:19:23.120 --> 00:19:25.660
What are you doing?

00:19:25.660 --> 00:19:27.040
Sherlock!

00:19:27.040 --> 00:19:30.160
We were drawing graffiti
and that guy just attacked us!

00:19:30.160 --> 00:19:32.620
Bring me a car!

00:19:32.620 --> 00:19:34.540
Or I'll kill the kid!

00:19:36.250 --> 00:19:38.040
Let me handle this.

00:19:38.040 --> 00:19:41.000
Moriarty.

00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:42.750
Stop this!

00:19:42.750 --> 00:19:46.700
You're not going to make anyone happy this way!

00:19:46.700 --> 00:19:48.080
Is he okay?

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:51.290
Is that Moran's son?

00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:52.160
Captain...

00:19:52.160 --> 00:19:56.620
Back off, or I'll really kill him...

00:19:56.620 --> 00:20:01.540
There's still time to stop
before there's no going back!

00:20:01.540 --> 00:20:04.000
You... You...

00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:06.830
Now let him go!

00:20:06.830 --> 00:20:08.910
Saizo Kumogakure!

00:20:12.910 --> 00:20:17.040
8020463840!

00:20:38.620 --> 00:20:40.620
Nice catch, huh?

00:20:42.330 --> 00:20:43.620
Wow!

00:20:43.620 --> 00:20:46.370
Way to go, Captain!

00:20:53.500 --> 00:20:55.290
You were so cool!

00:20:55.290 --> 00:20:58.580
You were like a superhero!

00:20:58.580 --> 00:21:00.200
Thanks...

00:21:01.040 --> 00:21:09.910
"Kabukicho's Hero Detective"

00:21:04.950 --> 00:21:07.540
Now let him go!

00:21:09.910 --> 00:21:13.000
Wow, look at these view numbers.

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:16.080
He's on TV, too! Look!

00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:19.040
"A Hero Detective is Born?!"

00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:19.040
Moririn's so cool!

00:21:19.330 --> 00:21:23.120
That'll get Moran more than a few votes.

00:21:23.120 --> 00:21:26.580
I can't believe so many people
are interested in a hero detective...

00:21:26.580 --> 00:21:28.410
Hey, Mori-ri-rin!

00:21:28.410 --> 00:21:31.700
It's me, Gokkun. I saw you on TV.

00:21:28.410 --> 00:21:29.950
If I'd known this was gonna happen,

00:21:29.950 --> 00:21:33.540
I would've sucked up to him more.

00:21:31.700 --> 00:21:33.540
Want to get dinner?

00:21:33.540 --> 00:21:36.750
Huh? Hello! Hello!

00:21:36.750 --> 00:21:39.950
Moririn's so cool!

00:21:39.950 --> 00:21:43.410
Moriarty's amazing, huh?

00:21:43.410 --> 00:21:45.410
What are you looking at?

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:51.700
"Serial Killer Commits Suicide in Prison"

00:21:54.200 --> 00:21:58.080
An update on the robbery at the Kabukicho 11-7.

00:21:58.080 --> 00:22:05.080
"Suspect Saizo Kumogakure Has Died"

00:21:58.080 --> 00:22:00.370
Saizo Kumogakure, the suspect,

00:22:00.370 --> 00:22:03.870
jumped off a roof during
his escape, hitting his head.

00:22:03.870 --> 00:22:07.160
He was confirmed dead at a nearby hospital.

00:22:07.160 --> 00:22:08.870
Tokyo 7th Prison...

00:22:07.160 --> 00:22:08.870
He was another of the escapees

00:22:08.870 --> 00:22:12.080
from Tokyo 7th Prison.

00:22:12.080 --> 00:22:17.160
Their leader, Albert Trevor, remains at large...

00:22:24.700 --> 00:22:27.250
This is kind of boring.

00:23:59.870 --> 00:24:04.870
"Lots of Animals"

00:23:59.870 --> 00:24:04.870
What does "Monster, Give Back the Sound" mean?

00:24:04.870 --> 00:24:06.830
"Find the Right Detective for You"
